   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output 8.2. Increased capacity of member States to improve governance and sustainability of social protection systems</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">In September 2021, the executive regulation of the recently issued social insurance and 2019 pension law 148/2019 was approved by the prime minister. The executive regulation will accelerate the implementation of the new social insurance and pension law which is a more inclusive and covers different types of workers, including informal workers, and will help increase the coverage of the social protection system in Egypt. 

In June 2021, as a requirement under the social insurance and pension law of 2019, and to ensure its successful implementation and better financial governance and planning for the social insurance system, the &quot;experts committee at the National Organization for Social Insurance&#x201D; was formed. 
The merge of the two pension funds (GSIF and PSIF) has been implemented since February of 2021 according to the new social insurance and pension law and started in some governorates including Sharkia and Cairo to improve and enhance the consistency and sustainability of the social insurance system. The ILO has been supporting the Ministry of Social Solidarity on the social insurance and pension reform and the Government of Egypt since 2014 based on a first ILO/MoSS Protocol of Cooperation (2014-2018) on the reform of the social insurance system in Egypt, which was renewed for the period 2019-2022. The ILO Protocol also introduced the SPF assessment and initial steps were undertaken for using the UN SPF as a building block for the formulation of a national social protection strategy for Egypt. 
During these years of cooperation, technical consultations with the involved ministries and institutions were held until a consensus was reached about the social insurance and pensions system reform directions. The ILO has provided technical support to the drafting of the new social insurance and pension law. Within the legal review, ILO Cairo advised the MoSS on how to revise the draft law to comply with social protection minimum standards Convention 102. The ILO has continued to support MoSS since the adoption of the law 148/2019 in August 2019  for the drafting of the Executive Regulations, which were finalized and submitted to the prime minister for approval.
Formation of the &quot;experts committee at the National Organization for Social Insurance&#x201D; according to the new law and build its capacity on actuarial work using the new ILO online pension model:
In June and July 2021, the ILO organized a training to the experts committee and the actuarial team at NOSI on the new ILO online actuarial pension model and provided the participants with access to the online model to help them better understand the model and how it can be used for different actuarial work.
ILO provided technical support for the administrative merge of the two pension funds through submitting a technical note regarding the administrative merge.</narrative>
